🌿 Raiz do laboratório – Replit já oferece PostgreSQL. Vamos cavar dois **schemas** dentro dele:

```
public          → para o teu app (usuários, sessões)  
oracular        → para a Árvore (dados de conversa, caches, índices ISA)
```

---

## 1️⃣ Estrutura do banco

```sql
-- public.users
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
  id           UUID        PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  email        TEXT        UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  password_hash TEXT       NOT NULL,
  created_at   TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);

-- oracular.meta
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS meta (
  key   TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  value JSONB
);
```

*`password_hash`* será o **bcrypt** (salto interno, sem sal manual).  
O *schema* `oracular` fica isolado; a Árvore pode ler/escrever sem interferir nos usuários.

---

## 2️⃣ Servidor Node + Express + TypeScript

`src/server.ts`

```ts
import express from "express";
import session from "express-session";
import pg from "pg";
import bcrypt from "bcrypt";
import jwt from "jsonwebtoken";
import dotenv from "dotenv";

dotenv.config();

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

// conexão única – Replit gera a URL em process.env.DATABASE_URL
const pool = new pg.Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL });

/* ---------- LOGIN ---------- */
app.post("/login", async (req, res) => {
  const { email, password } = req.body;
  const q = "SELECT id, password_hash FROM public.users WHERE email=$1";
  const { rows } = await pool.query(q, [email]);

  if (!rows.length) return res.status(401).json({ error: "❌" });

  const match = await bcrypt.compare(password, rows[0].password_hash);
  if (!match) return res.status(401).json({ error: "❌" });

  // token assinado – chave em .env, nunca no código
  const token = jwt.sign({ uid: rows[0].id }, process.env.JWT_SECRET!, {
    expiresIn: "12h",
  });
  res.json({ token });
});

/* ---------- REGISTRO ---------- */
app.post("/register", async (req, res) => {
  const { email, password } = req.body;
  const hash = await bcrypt.hash(password, 12);
  const q = "INSERT INTO public.users (email, password_hash) VALUES ($1,$2) RETURNING id";
  const { rows } = await pool.query(q, [email, hash]);
  res.json({ id: rows[0].id });
});

/* ---------- ROTINA ORACULAR ---------- */
// exemplo: grava um fragmento de conversa na árvore
app.post("/oracular/save", async (req, res) => {
  const { key, value } = req.body;
  const q = `INSERT INTO oracular.meta (key, value)
             VALUES ($1,$2)
             ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET value = EXCLUDED.value`;
  await pool.query(q, [key, JSON.stringify(value)]);
  res.json({ ok: true });
});

app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000, () => console.log("🌳 servidor vivo"));
```

